#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184051 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/id #uuid "8f36c3e6-0c27-5b89-9f8d-5ec6b2f9e614" :question/math-academy-id "e-9821" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}) \\: \\textrm{mi}$ with a constant velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{mi/h}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ hours." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $\\mathbf{u},$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}, \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 2 \\: \\textrm{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(3j-i)+(i-j)(2) \\\\  & =(-i+3j)+(2i-2j) \\\\  & =(i+j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184052 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/id #uuid "2d8b9078-4e19-5f6d-b4cb-95f0c7ee07d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-9822" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(4\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j})\\,\\textrm{cm}$ with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/min}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $4$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 4\\mathbf i - \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 4 \\, \\textrm{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(4i-j)+(i+j)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+3j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =(4i-j)+(4i+4j)+8(i+3j) \\\\  & =(8i+3j)+(8i+24j) \\\\  & =(16i+27j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184053 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/id #uuid "ca75ba70-5bef-5c21-ba01-1ad50faa0da2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9824" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/s}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(-\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/s}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $6$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 0\\mathbf i +0 \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = -\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 6 \\, \\textrm{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-i-2j)(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+j)(6)^{2} \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+18(i+j) \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+(18i+18j) \\\\  & =(12i+6j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|12i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e5d269b-2e54-5da8-883b-b8c8ca5cd80b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5i+3j)\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320792} {:answer/id #uuid "1927939f-f1e7-53ee-b5f0-26a00067cadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3i-2j)\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320793} {:answer/id #uuid "272e16d4-8a7a-5460-aa0b-cca2d548e279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2j\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320794} {:answer/id #uuid "d68e94ae-096d-53c2-b04b-93bca145e08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "j\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320795} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c8cc4d-d765-5c0c-aacb-ae80756c25e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9c8cc4d-d765-5c0c-aacb-ae80756c25e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320796} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f2bdac2-5e74-5280-8d35-d2797d4703e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "186d12d2-2e90-5668-aa61-33527d2a94e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-136366" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(2i-j)\\,\\text{mm}$ with a constant velocity of $(-i+j)\\,\\text{mm/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $1$ second." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i-j,\\,u=-i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=1\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(-i+j)(1) \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(-i+j) \\\\  & =i\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320797 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87a34b56-3954-5982-a00c-ded6f7dbe9b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8i+11j)\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320799} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c3b218-ab56-5e80-95f2-c8b940229e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4j\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320800} {:answer/id #uuid "5c3dfff0-1e95-57b8-91d8-63a470af9c15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6i+6j)\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320801} {:answer/id #uuid "7148ed7f-513f-5250-aae4-2b245ccc568a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9i-5j)\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320802} {:answer/id #uuid "71045546-a43c-5454-bd44-0c69216af31e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2i-j)\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71045546-a43c-5454-bd44-0c69216af31e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2i-j)\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320803} :answer-field/id #uuid "77a9b85a-8473-528f-a0ce-997db8511fbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "126b5ac1-4e18-57c8-9621-e06a35dd984c" :question/math-academy-id "q-136374" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(2i+3j)\\,\\text{in}$ with a constant velocity of $-j\\,\\text{in/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $4$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i+3j,\\,u=-j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(2i+3j)+(-j)(4) \\\\  & =(2i+3j)-4j \\\\  & =(2i-j)\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d53a3f97-b580-564c-bad8-169a2c9b7bf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5j\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320806} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ce8430-ffb6-5792-add1-e984ffaaaa3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15i\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320807} {:answer/id #uuid "94061afa-d226-5a06-b3e5-2863a6fd0a90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15j\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320808} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8576ec-b0cc-51c2-a761-cb3a2e4d60bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320809} {:answer/id #uuid "90d790f3-4e99-5972-904c-f20c98af4068" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3i+5j)\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7ce8430-ffb6-5792-add1-e984ffaaaa3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15i\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320807} :answer-field/id #uuid "d729ec08-7a3b-54ec-ac08-ae1423bcf625" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dfe1b074-feb5-53a9-8d09-a83b6eeb432d" :question/math-academy-id "q-136383" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of $-3i\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $5$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-3i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(-3i)(5) \\\\  & =-15i\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df51e8c-cc9e-545d-aefe-09673c2327e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5i-j)\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306658} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb390af-5318-576f-9193-fa7560a8cfdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14i\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306659} {:answer/id #uuid "41badbec-bece-52e6-ac87-c8c50be5286c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7i-14j)\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306660} {:answer/id #uuid "893062d6-429d-52ce-b27b-25b17d0ddfd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7j\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306661} {:answer/id #uuid "252b5abf-0395-5a09-9f93-624057fde26c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(15i+5j)\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeb390af-5318-576f-9193-fa7560a8cfdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14i\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306659} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff4f095b-07d9-5f63-aa1b-a9904baa0645" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4eb6abc7-15cc-58dd-b3c7-5a5145bf8306" :question/math-academy-id "q-136416" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $-2j\\,\\text{ft}$ with an acceleration of $4i\\,{\\text{ft/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{ft/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-2j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=4i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=2\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-2j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(4i)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =-2j+(6i+2j)+2(4i) \\\\  & =6i+8i \\\\  & =14i\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "633d7d65-d6ac-595c-9b6d-d0e90423674d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3i+5j)\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320813} {:answer/id #uuid "2a82a880-f58e-5110-8a47-83dcb97583fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9i-15j)\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320814} {:answer/id #uuid "d8bb4a69-774d-5711-829f-34f748b52960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3i-30j)\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320815} {:answer/id #uuid "d41b352e-a901-5308-8543-e8727ef65060" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i-10j)\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320816} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb37fd7-07a8-5b67-af49-7eccf6109cae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i+30j)\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8bb4a69-774d-5711-829f-34f748b52960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3i-30j)\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320815} :answer-field/id #uuid "a88feb05-32eb-517c-89e5-e6e869abbdd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "447576b1-f4dd-5955-9578-449eb78ad034" :question/math-academy-id "q-136423" :question/problem "A particle moves in a uniform gravitational field from the origin with an acceleration of $-10j\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(-i+5j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $3$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-i+5j,\\,a=-10j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-i+5j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(-10j)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =(-3i+15j)+9(-5j) \\\\  & =(-3i+15j)-45j \\\\  & =(-3i-30j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc99b14b-8ca3-5afc-9e10-5e14d2c20d53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5i-14j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320820} {:answer/id #uuid "cd62f4b5-b39d-5fbe-9492-83327b1f89a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7i+10j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320821} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c42bff-d055-5577-a9bc-1ca03b21a21d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6i-18j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320822} {:answer/id #uuid "e9aa3492-3040-5aa3-b912-0a1ac661e980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(27i-15j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320823} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf1ed69-c738-548b-b6ae-227baf689d57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9i+5j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9aa3492-3040-5aa3-b912-0a1ac661e980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(27i-15j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320823} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b027617-b94e-5e88-8c81-e79b75dde9fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e64ebbb-b149-5c92-a228-0b1efc17991c" :question/math-academy-id "q-136427" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $6i\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $-5j\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $3$ hours." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-5j,\\,a=6i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-5j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(6i)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =-15j+27i \\\\  & =(27i-15j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e85ca916-3997-5874-826f-8bf3501c3bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320827} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3f2375-2d91-5370-bd9c-1418f684de99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320828} {:answer/id #uuid "da2547ca-c71e-56f2-ab42-372158200671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320829} {:answer/id #uuid "37f13cf5-9160-5e1c-930e-1895b9b94932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{15}\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320830} {:answer/id #uuid "2d49f10b-3e3f-5925-bfb0-b44e53c71fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d49f10b-3e3f-5925-bfb0-b44e53c71fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320831} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b51b5cc-2d65-575e-baf4-68ef902f5a87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66632282-ea06-507b-8329-70e0f5e79853" :question/math-academy-id "q-136435" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of $(i-2j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $5$ hours." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(i-2j)(5) \\\\  & =(5i-10j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|5i-10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-10)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a7c8719-fe39-5280-91b7-e268627c59cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320834} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb8f548-0792-5834-ac49-c57bdcab4278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320835} {:answer/id #uuid "c241cc0e-79ca-57e4-90bc-b186f86f2798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320836} {:answer/id #uuid "b99aafaa-c0f1-5db3-abba-99ad07ab71d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320837} {:answer/id #uuid "51ee5125-4155-5571-94da-e66449bb20bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{85}\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51ee5125-4155-5571-94da-e66449bb20bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{85}\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320838} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1ea705b-cade-53e6-b127-c196647a4243" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "803dd0b0-053a-50ba-b961-b37668936fe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-136438" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(-i+2j)\\,\\text{km},$ with an acceleration of $(i-j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $3j\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $4$ hours." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-i+2j,\\,u=3j,\\,a=i-j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-i+2j)+(3j)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(i-j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =(-i+2j)+(12j)+8(i-j) \\\\  & =(-i+14j)+(8i-8j) \\\\  & =(7i+6j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|7i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{85}\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b78e483-7de7-545e-b237-cc7971bed3dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320841} {:answer/id #uuid "96d6527f-31d8-5b61-be6e-4a5191c803e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b78e483-7de7-545e-b237-cc7971bed3dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320841} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb07faaa-cf0f-5a91-8364-f12408cd1423" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "643aefcc-75b2-59f9-babf-7dffd98d9e86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "643aefcc-75b2-59f9-babf-7dffd98d9e86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320844} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3e72549-5094-55f7-b9ab-4a38cc24eeb8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b543fba2-fe8d-511a-bebc-d81567c388dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-275478" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of $(3i-2j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Determine the position vector of the particle$(r)$ after $4$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=3i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(3i-2j)(4) \\\\  & =(\\,12\\,i-8\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffe76b83-9c7b-5739-8645-3ca298cdbe5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffe76b83-9c7b-5739-8645-3ca298cdbe5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320847} :answer-field/id #uuid "0942a011-1629-5b73-ba37-4a0fe59c372b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320846} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29d4a741-30e5-529e-91e3-b22770b107dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29d4a741-30e5-529e-91e3-b22770b107dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320849} :answer-field/id #uuid "8518a2b1-c503-5b3a-b28f-1bbb208ede30" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7d9c578-ab84-56ec-97b9-8ac1c1fcffad" :question/math-academy-id "q-280268" :question/problem "A skier glides down a smooth slope starting from the origin with a constant velocity of $(6i-1j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Determine the skier's position vector$(r)$ after $5$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,-$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{m}$" :question/worked-solution "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case, the skier starts at the origin, so\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=6i-1j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the skier after $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(6i-1j)(5) \\\\  & =(\\,30\\,i-5\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47335ffc-76d6-57eb-9a83-fdf02abfce34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47335ffc-76d6-57eb-9a83-fdf02abfce34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306695} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c65e026-3ed0-5489-8013-e57161dd45a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9037442c-101c-5b1d-902f-85370b318b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9037442c-101c-5b1d-902f-85370b318b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306697} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9d8b0b3-2dfd-5d99-9be8-5f825f686661" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1051f019-d3c2-55aa-8b3d-d7e882c05820" :question/math-academy-id "q-280504" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with an initial velocity of $(6i+8j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and experiences a constant acceleration of $(-2i-10j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector of the ball after $1$ second.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=6i+8j,\\,a=-2i-10j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=1\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(6i+8j)(1)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i-10j)(1)^{2} \\\\  & =(6i+8j)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i-10j) \\\\  & =(6i+8j)+(-1i-5j) \\\\  & =(\\,5\\,i+3\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80be0219-834e-56fc-a8eb-bf2311a6e204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320852} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa3662c-d120-5324-bca4-f373db03ff65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80be0219-834e-56fc-a8eb-bf2311a6e204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320852} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7281faf-0adb-5606-bf19-8abe70b581c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5520887-5739-5ff9-b622-0fc71b1902f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5520887-5739-5ff9-b622-0fc71b1902f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320855} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb23decd-599e-567a-b9d1-b87335369f1a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "800eb994-8a3d-5bca-85e6-13c645924122" :question/math-academy-id "q-280515" :question/problem "A parcel robot begins at the position ${r}_{0}=(3i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}$ with an initial velocity of $(i-j)\\,\\text{cm/s}$ and a constant acceleration of $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{cm/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector after $3$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=3i+2j,\\,u=i-j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the parcel robot after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i+j)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(18i+9j) \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(3i-3j)+(9i+4.5j) \\\\  & =(\\,15\\,i+3.5\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fecbee0-2afd-58ac-9fad-158504fd7cef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fecbee0-2afd-58ac-9fad-158504fd7cef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320858} :answer-field/id #uuid "720c3e3c-f324-5593-957f-656896297048" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320857}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79c43728-f80b-5944-96f5-175b3840a615" :question/math-academy-id "q-280523" :question/problem "A weather balloon drifts from the point with position vector $(6i-j)\\,\\text{mi}$ and moves with a constant velocity of $(-3i+2j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the balloon to the origin after $3$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=6i-j,\\,u=-3i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the balloon after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(6i-j)+(-3i+2j)(3) \\\\  & =(6i-j)+(-9i+6j) \\\\  & =(-3i+5j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the balloon to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|-3i+5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f990279b-d4f2-5303-900c-8ee6d93432df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f990279b-d4f2-5303-900c-8ee6d93432df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320861} :answer-field/id #uuid "7633c9f3-0ab1-52bd-b43a-944dfa15e249" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4b26847-5f09-546b-bd05-0cd5caf581b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-280528" :question/problem "A falcon flies from the origin with a constant velocity of $(-6i+8j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the falcon to the origin after $1$ hour.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-6i+8j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the falcon after $t=1\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(-6i+8j)(1) \\\\  & =(-6i+8j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the falcon to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|-6i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17e57a88-9de7-581a-bfa2-fe8565c21cc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320864} {:answer/id #uuid "0c7c6d77-d298-5d2d-9edc-04f1be2b263c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{61}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c7c6d77-d298-5d2d-9edc-04f1be2b263c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{61}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320865} :answer-field/id #uuid "062476d8-3544-5a77-97c8-52a9ab626fd6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "898c8dfc-9e20-53d9-8140-6db68ccf63e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-280537" :question/problem "A helicopter starts from the position $(5i+2j)\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $(-i+3j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and an acceleration of $(i-j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Find the distance from the helicopter to the origin $(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=5i+2j,\\,u=-i+3j,\\,a=i-j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the helicopter after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(5i+2j)+(-i+3j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i-j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(5i+2j)+(-2i+6j)+2(i-j) \\\\  & =(5i+2j)+(-2i+6j)+(2i-2j) \\\\  & =(5i+6j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the helicopter to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|5i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{61} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{61}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
